Answer: One solution is to only look at a small substructure when checking band gaps.

We look at single cations and anions. If the cation is surrounded completely by the anions we check if the bandgap of the cation (such as C) is larger or smaller than the bandgap of the anion ( such as Ga or Cs). Here we recognise that the Ga/Cs anions do not influence the bandgaps.

So in the Python code below for each cation we loop over each position and check if the largest overlap is bigger or smaller than 0.1. If the overlap is bigger we continue and check the bigger bandgap.

\begin{code}
poscar = '/path/to/poscar'
eigenvectors = DistGeom.get_eigen(poscar)

cations = set(map(lambda x: x.name, eigenvectors[:,0]))
anions = set(map(lambda x: x.name, eigenvectors[1,:]) | cations)

for cation in cations:
    anions_seen = set()
    for i,l in enumerate(eigenvectors[:,i]):
        overlaps = []
        for j,r in enumerate(l):
            if i <= j:
                overlaps.append(np.abs(l[:j].distance(l[i:j+1]) - r.distance(r[i:j+1])))
        if sum(overlaps) <= 0.1:
            anions_seen.add(anions.pop())
             # if i and j are both in anions we can now set the bigger band gap
            if sum(overlaps) >= 0.9:
                bandgaps = eignevectors[{cation:i},{cations.pop() : j}]
                    if eigenvectors[cations.pop()][j].real > eigenvectors[cations.pop()][i].real:
                        print(bandgaps)
    # other cations without band gaps
    anions_seen.add(anions.pop())
    for j,r in enumerate(eigenvectors[:,j]):
        overlaps = []
        for i,l in enumerate(r):
            if i <= j:
                overlaps.append(np.abs(l[:i].distance(l[i+1:j+1]) - r.distance(r[i+1:j+1])))
        anions_seen.add(anions[i].pop())
        #if anions.pop() is not in the set we set the bigger band gap
        if sum(overlaps) >= 0.9:
            bandgaps = eigevectors[{cations : i},{cations.pop() : j}]
            if eigenvectors[cations.pop()][j].real > eigenvectors[cations.pop()][i].real:
                print(bandgaps)
\end{code}

