\strong{Length Unit}

Length unit define the used unit for your result output. By default output get in m that mean m of Diameter per side. But I would like to change to have result in \strong{bohr}. Therefore don't mistake unit and the length or diameter number because they change when you change unit.

To be clear about length unit follow this:
\begin{itemize}
\item If you have something = to m, that equal 1 \strong{\em{(means one unit of Pauling Radius)}}
\item If you have something = to nm, that equal 10^{-8} \strong{\em{(means one unit of Angstrom)}}
\item If you have something = to Å, that equal 10^{-10} \strong{\em{(means one unit of Bohr)}}
\end{itemize}

For example in the output file `str_881224_2.out`

\begin{code}
