Answer: As suggested by PMR, it is best to define a macro row colour before using it:

\begin{code}
\NewDocumentCommand{\mycolrowstart}{ O{} D}
    {
    \colorbox{D}{#1}
    \lineunder[D]{1em}{#1}
}
\end{code}

In that way, one mostly does not need the additional manual setup etc. of `\OverrideColorSelection`. Furthermore, this allows one to use special colour codes to define a desired row colour for some reason or other.

