Answer: The femto-SOURCE wrapper script is a full fledged parallel CDF library implementation.  The 'src' file and the wrapper manage all of the materials.  Yours are references to common materials that are stored as functions in femto-SOURCE.  Except for the band gap in elastic constants, for which they are stored in hdf5 files, everything else in your code can't vary for different structures.  The wrapper, library functions, and chimera.hdf5 call these material functions:

\begin{code}
get_struct_material()
    get the material structure for this simulation.
    Return the material structure as a list of lists in the form:
        { solid_density:0.01_kgm^-3; rigid_density:20_kgm^-3...};

get_struct_one_absorb_pos()
    Get the [i,j,k] vector a that makes the following transformation for band gap:
        [{ j:5.0604; i:5.9156; k:0.0}
        { j:0.0000 i:0.0000 k:0.0}
        { j:0.0000 i:0.0000 k:0.0}
        { j:0.0000 i:0.0000 k:0.0}
        { j:0.0000 i:0.0000 k:0.0}
        { j:0.0000 i:0.0000 k:0.0}
        { j:0.0000 i:0.0000 k:0.0}
        { j:0.0000 i:0.0000 k:0.0}
        { j:0.0000 i:0.0000 k:0.0}
        { j:0.0000 i:0.0000 k:0.0}]

set_struct_one_absorb_pos(struct_one)
     Update the [i,j,k] vector for band gap.
     Change the vector struct_one at 0 points, where [i,j,k] = <>=, <...>, >.  struct_one is guaranteed to be a list of lists in the form [[m1, m2,...],[n1, n2, ...]..] where n1 or n2 is incomming.
\end{code}

So, your materials data files should look something like [this](https://github.com/eCDF/eCDF/blob/master/share/src/sftymaterials.dat).  NOTE, I put two columns of symmetry information under the source column- you should have one, the other is my addition.  Also, your band gap data file should be different, as some of the formulae that generate the band gap data may have changed.  Here's an example (updated simplified by NerdyResidue from a source on my machine).  Note the symmetry information at the top and the band gap in the field/value column.  I update this regularly.

\begin{code}
[ITEM]
SYS = [Material identificator]
source = [#](2)
Number fields = [#]
LMin = {Name= Li2O2}
LMax = {Li2O2}
LIn = {Li2O2}
LOut = {Li2O2}
LTons = {0.12647,0.1233}
LTons2 = {0.1243022}
LDOS = {0.1531,0.386,0.1531}
LComp = {LOut-LIn=0.75,LOut-LDOS=0}
[ENDITEM]
/ITEM
\end{code}

