Answer: Mostly, LaTeX documents are divided into Sections, Chapters, Sequences and Pages (and within these, sections have their own headers). Entries to your table (basically a list of entries into one line) will be inserted in the middle of a line within a `*cell` environment.

So for a data table, you want to after the `[Table]` declaration something like:

\begin{code}
[Table]
@beforehand{
    \centering
}
\end{code}

