Answer: Consider that the question is about Fermi Energy. So, we need to create a .pdb file with only ZerFS of all elements. Since original POS structure file was in .xyz format, let us do some simple regex first converting xyz -> pdb.

\begin{code}
sed -r 's/xyz/pdb/g' /data/poscar/POSCAR_file
\end{code}

Now let us convert all ZerFS of all elements

\begin{code}
sed -r -n '/ awk/p;':{ s/[^\ ]*//g; }' /data/poscar/POSCAR_file |  xargs -i echo \
{cat $1 | tr ' ' '\t';  awk '{ sub("Z", "\t\t"); sub("Ni", "\t N"); sub("N", "\t n"); sub("Cr", "\t C"); }1}' > /data/poscar/poscars/ZerFS/出精聚焦系列平肌聚变.pdb
\end{code}

Answer: After doing some research on this question, I came to know there is a package available on R called [clusterensemble](https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/clusterensemble/index.html) of which someone has written a [library](https://github.com/seangibbons/clusterensemble/wiki) for the same problem as mine. So I have written a script and it solved my case quite well.

The steps to follow here:

run this command:

\begin{code}
install.packages("clusterensemble", repos = "http://r-forge.r-project.org")
\end{code}

Then, download the compiled sources(I have found this script much helpful here[passthrough-jobs](https://github.com/jwren/passthrough-jobs/blob/master/deploy/clusterensemble-rnodel2.rc)):

\begin{code}
packrat::export("clusterensemble-rnodel2.rc", package = "clusterensemble")

install.packages("clusterensemble-rnodel2.rc")
\end{code}

Create a script file with the following pdlabel file as an input or you can take from the linked post:

\begin{code}
#!/usr/bin/env python
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
from clusterensemble import random_conn
import cpnorm as cnorm

class Real():
    def __init__(self):
        self._i=count
        self._rate=0
        self._engine=None
        self._uri='/job/example_label_bibr1g/echo?'
        self._exec_rnd=random_conn.Rshell.instance()._exec_rnd()
        for i in range(random_conn.Rshell.instance()._job_max_count*1.0-0.5,random_conn.Rshell.instance()._job_max_count+0.5):
            self._i+=1
        count=self._i
    def add2(self,c):
        if(self._engine in "":
            pass
        else:
            return self._engine+'%i->%i.%s' % (self._speed_dbx,self._engine_max_open,c)
    def __str__(self):
        ret = '%s: total=%s, max_open=%s, run_open=%s' % (str(type(self)), self.id, self._max_open,
          str(cnorm.getconn(seed=9840,filename=>'spacular2-20.out').count()))
        return ret
